# New page objects

Read `LoginPage`, `SuccessfulLoginPage`, and `BasePage` before adding a page. `ExceptionsPage` is the example for elements that appear after a click. Do not copy a method whose name and locator disagree: `isInstructionsNoLongerDisplayedAfterWait` waits on the edit button, not `#instructions`.

## Class

- Package `com.practicetestautomation.pageobjects`, file under `src/main/java/com/practicetestautomation/pageobjects/`.
- `public class <Name>Page extends BasePage`.
- Constructor: `public <Name>Page(WebDriver driver) { super(driver); }`.
- Import `By`, `WebDriver`, and `WebElement` only when the file uses them. Do not import TestNG. Do not use `PageFactory` or `@FindBy`.
- Do not create a `WebDriver` or a `WebDriverWait`. `BasePage` already stores `driver` and a 10-second `wait`.

## Locators

- Declare `private By` fields before the constructor, as `LoginPage` and `SuccessfulLoginPage` do, with a `Locator` suffix: `usernameInputLocator`, `addButtonLocator`.
- Prefer `By.id` when the element has an id. Use `By.linkText` for a link such as `Log out`. Scope an xpath to one row when the same id is repeated, as `row2InputLocator` does.
- Keep the locator on the field. Do not call `By.id` or `By.xpath` inside a method.

## Methods

- A page opened by its own URL gets `public void visit()` that calls `super.visit` with the full `https://practicetestautomation.com/...` URL. A page reached only from another page, such as `SuccessfulLoginPage`, has no `visit()`.
- Public names: `click...` for clicks, `enter...(String)` for typing, `get...` for visible text, `is...Displayed` for a check, and `load` to wait until a landmark is visible.
- Return `void` for a click, `String` for text, `boolean` for a display check, or the next page when the action navigates. `executeLogin` returns `new SuccessfulLoginPage(driver)`.
- Pass typed text in from the test. Do not store usernames, passwords, or expected messages on the page.
- Do not call `Assert`. The test owns every assertion.

## Waits

Call the `BasePage` helpers. Do not add another `WebDriverWait` or import `ExpectedConditions` in a page class.

- The element is already on the page: `driver.findElement(locator)` for `sendKeys`, `clear`, and `click` (`enterUsername`, `clickAddButton`).
- The field may already contain text: `clear()` then `sendKeys`, as `enterTextInRowOne` does. A field that starts empty uses `sendKeys` only.
- Text appears after an action: `waitForElement(locator).getText()` (`getErrorMessage`, `getSuccessMessage`).
- A click must wait until the control is enabled: `waitForElementToBeClickable(locator).click()` (`clickEditButton`).
- The next page is ready: `waitForElement(locator)` inside `load()`.
- Boolean "visible now": `isDisplayed(locator)`. It returns false on `NoSuchElementException`.
- Boolean "becomes visible within 10 seconds": `waitForIsDisplayed(locator)`. It returns false on timeout. Name the method `is...DisplayedAfterWait`.
- Boolean "goes away within 10 seconds": `waitForInvisibilityOfElement(locator)`. It returns false on timeout. The locator must be the element named by the method.

Put a new shared wait on `BasePage`. A page class calls that method instead of copying it.
